{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>They are my sons whom Elohim has given me בָּזֶה (in this).</b> He used the word בָּזֶה because he [Jacob] asked him, 'Who are these?' — meaning they are not worthy of blessing. For he said, מִבֶּטֶן מִי יָצְאוּ אֵלֶּה — meaning that they will say אֵלֶּה אֱלֹהֶיךָ of the calf that Jeroboam made. And Joseph answered, 'They are my sons' — in any case they are my sons, and from my side they are worthy of blessing. And as for what will come forth from them — Ahab and Jeroboam — that is because Elohim gave them to me בָּזֶה, here in Egypt, and their mother is an Egyptian, the daughter of Poti-phera priest of On, which is to say a priest of idolatry; therefore there will come forth from her in the future sons such as these, worshippers of idolatry. But from my side they are worthy of blessing, for if not, why did HaShem bless Isaac, seeing that Esau and Jacob came forth from him because Rebecca was the daughter of Bethuel the Aramean? Rather, surely the Holy One, blessed be He, does not take account of the blemished seed, and blessed him on account of the holy seed that is worthy of blessing. So shall you too bless them, for from my side they are worthy of blessing, for ״בַּאֲשֶׁר הוּא שָׁם״ (Genesis 21:17) — all of them ״זֶרַע בֵּרַךְ ה׳״ (Isaiah 61:9)." "<b>And he said: Bring them now, I pray you, אֵלַי (to me).</b> He used the word אֵלַי to indicate that one may properly learn from me — for on my account my father was blessed, and the Holy One, blessed be He, did not take account of Esau; meaning, let those who are blessed be like me; therefore ״קָחֶם אֵלָי.״ And with the word ״נָא״ he indicated the present tense, like ״הִנֵּה נָא יָדַעְתִּי״ (Genesis 12:11), whose meaning is 'now.' And he means to say: I am about to bless them according to the time of now, for now they are all righteous, and I will not take account of the future. ״וַיְבָרֶךְ אוֹתָם בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא לֵאמֹר״ (Genesis 48:20) — according to what they were on that day, and he did not take account of the future, of what would come from their seed, for a person is judged only according to his deeds of now. Another interpretation: he said אֵלַי to say, they trace their lineage to me, for the father's family is primary, but the mother's family is not called family."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:13.467018947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}